WEBVTT

00:58.559 --> 00:59.393
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION

00:59.477 --> 01:00.978
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED SAFELY
WITH SUPERVISION

01:02.855 --> 01:05.024
As we speak, it's a foul ball.

01:05.107 --> 01:06.692
The tension is high right now.

01:06.776 --> 01:08.736
The pitcher looks really shaken up.

01:08.819 --> 01:10.905
His breaking balls
are in the middle of the zone.

01:13.783 --> 01:17.036
After getting into a jam with two outs,
bases loaded in the bottom of the 9th,

01:17.119 --> 01:18.370
the pitcher's being pulled.

01:20.623 --> 01:22.374
And here comes Park Gi-yoon.

01:22.458 --> 01:24.251
SAEUM is putting their trust

01:24.335 --> 01:27.129
into their veteran to get the final out.

01:27.213 --> 01:30.591
Park Gi-yoon steps onto the mound
looking visibly flushed.

01:32.259 --> 01:33.844
The score is 5-2.

01:33.928 --> 01:37.807
SAEUM Sis only one out away
from winning the Korean Series.

01:37.890 --> 01:41.852
But the question is, will they be able
to get out of this crisis?

01:43.771 --> 01:46.190
The pitch bounces in the plate. Ball one.

01:46.273 --> 01:47.650
He's feeling the pressure.

01:47.733 --> 01:49.318
His body's way too tense right now.

01:49.401 --> 01:52.488
I warned you,
you absolutely can't be late today!

01:52.571 --> 01:54.490
Did you get off the bus? Where are you?

01:54.573 --> 01:55.407
Ji-yoon.

01:55.491 --> 01:57.243
I'm going on a trip.

01:57.326 --> 01:59.870
Sorry, I know you said
you had something to tell me.

01:59.954 --> 02:02.873
The ball goes over the left field wall!

02:02.957 --> 02:04.166
That's a home run!

02:04.250 --> 02:06.502
-A walk-off home run!
-It went over the wall.

02:06.585 --> 02:08.170
-This is the worst.
-Unbelievable!

02:08.254 --> 02:10.548
And that's how this ballgame ends!

02:10.631 --> 02:12.591
This is the stuff movies are made of.

02:15.010 --> 02:17.763
FINAL
SAEUM (LOSS) 5 : 6 KP (WIN)

02:26.522 --> 02:27.857
JI-YOON & GA-EUL

02:48.878 --> 02:55.885
WILL YOU MARRY ME?

02:59.305 --> 03:01.015
Even when you get ghosted…

03:03.267 --> 03:06.520
8 MONTHS LATER

03:07.563 --> 03:08.647
…you still go to work.

03:18.365 --> 03:19.366
Even when you're unwell…

03:24.413 --> 03:26.832
Even when your family passes away…

03:39.553 --> 03:41.221
Even when you meet a complete dirtbag…

03:48.312 --> 03:50.731
What, you want me
to charge that for you too?

03:56.236 --> 03:57.154
…you still go to work.

03:59.490 --> 04:01.659
SAFETY ALERT
HEAVY RAIN WARNING IN EFFECT

04:02.242 --> 04:03.577
SAFETY ALERT
HEAVY RAIN WARNING IN EFFECT

04:05.621 --> 04:06.538
DONGNIMMUN

04:06.622 --> 04:09.667
HEAVY RAIN WARNING IN EFFECT

04:13.212 --> 04:17.216
HEAVY RAIN WARNING IN EFFECT
STAY INSIDE, SAFETY FIRST

04:28.352 --> 04:30.396
In this hellish work life,

04:31.021 --> 04:33.023
will hope ever show itself?

05:22.740 --> 05:24.658
Where are we going?

05:26.535 --> 05:27.369
To work.

05:27.953 --> 05:28.787
What?

05:39.923 --> 05:45.471
EPISODE 1
EVEN IF THE SKY FALLS, STILL CLOCKING IN!

05:56.106 --> 05:58.108
What heavy rain? It's perfectly sunny.

06:06.533 --> 06:07.785
Why did I come so early?

06:26.303 --> 06:27.971
Breaking! Three-No-Man is coming!

06:30.641 --> 06:32.684
Three-No-Man?
Wasn't he over at the US office?

06:32.768 --> 06:35.646
Wow, my commute just got spicy
for the first time in ages.

06:35.729 --> 06:38.524
Haha. Anyway, brace yourselves.
I sense a bloodbath coming.

06:38.607 --> 06:40.692
"Three-No-Man"? Who are you talking about?

06:41.360 --> 06:43.070
-Geez, you're really out of the loop.
-Hello.

06:43.153 --> 06:44.154
Hello.

06:45.364 --> 06:46.532
-Cha Ji-yoon.
-You're here.

06:47.074 --> 06:48.992
I knew you'd come.
Got these for a BOGO deal.

06:49.076 --> 06:51.495
Thanks. But don't you know Kang Si-woo?

06:52.204 --> 06:53.080
Kang Si-woo?

06:54.289 --> 06:56.041
Oh, that legendary workaholic?

06:56.125 --> 06:58.293
Exactly. That Kang Si-woo is Three-No-Man.

06:58.377 --> 06:59.461
I see.

06:59.545 --> 07:00.504
"I see"?

07:01.380 --> 07:02.422
No smile.

07:02.506 --> 07:03.799
No people.

07:03.882 --> 07:04.842
No sorry.

07:04.925 --> 07:06.176
This is Kang Si-woo.

07:06.260 --> 07:09.179
I requested those materials by today,
but they're not in my inbox.

07:09.263 --> 07:10.639
Did my request get lost,

07:10.722 --> 07:13.016
or are you simply a slow worker?

07:13.100 --> 07:14.935
The man with a cold face
that never smiles.

07:15.018 --> 07:16.854
He rarely socializes with other people

07:16.937 --> 07:19.898
and never apologizes first,
whether to those above or below him.

07:19.982 --> 07:22.484
We call him "Three-No-Man."

07:24.778 --> 07:25.988
Doors closing.

07:27.239 --> 07:30.033
Wait! Hang on!

07:30.117 --> 07:31.577
Oh, come on.

07:41.753 --> 07:42.671
This is Kang Si-woo.

07:42.754 --> 07:46.175
The man behind the legendary 100%
task force project success rate!

07:46.258 --> 07:48.135
He was made manager after just five years

07:48.218 --> 07:49.803
after two special promotions!

07:49.887 --> 07:53.098
But behind Three-No-Man
Kang Si-woo's success

07:53.182 --> 07:54.850
lies the blood of countless people.

07:54.933 --> 07:56.268
I'll be back tomorrow.

07:56.977 --> 07:57.853
Yes.

08:01.857 --> 08:03.400
Have you been reading martial arts novels?

08:03.483 --> 08:06.445
Why would there be a bloodbath
at an electronics company?

08:06.528 --> 08:08.447
When Mr. Kang's task forces are disbanded,

08:08.530 --> 08:11.200
the team members vanish without a trace.
Didn't you know?

08:11.283 --> 08:12.326
What?

08:12.409 --> 08:13.994
Oh, man.

08:14.077 --> 08:16.663
I heard some even took leave
to get therapy.

08:16.747 --> 08:18.123
Hey, No-ah.

08:22.628 --> 08:25.088
The group chat's been blowing up
about Three-No-Man.

08:25.172 --> 08:26.215
I know.

08:26.298 --> 08:29.051
How big a deal is he that everyone's
losing it before he's even here?

08:29.134 --> 08:30.636
Is he hot?

08:30.719 --> 08:32.387
Gosh, pay attention to office politics.

08:32.471 --> 08:33.972
Keep your eyes and ears open.

08:34.056 --> 08:36.350
There are 100,000 people at this company.

08:36.433 --> 08:39.770
How are you supposed to work if you
stuff your head with every little rumor?

08:39.853 --> 08:42.439
Come on, what's wrong with you all?

08:43.482 --> 08:45.651
Why do you keep talking nonsense?

08:47.527 --> 08:50.697
What the heck are we supposed to do
if you suspend the production?

08:53.158 --> 08:55.494
Hey. Launch is just around the corner.

08:55.577 --> 08:58.205
This is when we should be
compromising and pulling together,

08:58.288 --> 08:59.122
but you're…

09:00.123 --> 09:01.124
Huh?

09:02.334 --> 09:03.919
Then what about me?

09:04.002 --> 09:05.379
What am I supposed to do?

09:05.796 --> 09:06.713
Hello?

09:06.797 --> 09:07.631
Hel--

09:08.298 --> 09:09.132
Oh, this…

09:12.344 --> 09:13.845
Is something wrong, sir?

09:13.929 --> 09:17.891
The researchers and the factory workers
are at a standoff right now.

09:17.975 --> 09:19.977
The production line has stopped!

09:20.060 --> 09:21.687
What? Why?

09:21.770 --> 09:23.146
That's what I'd like to ask you.

09:23.981 --> 09:26.316
Just how did you people handle this work

09:26.400 --> 09:29.236
for things to blow up like this

09:29.319 --> 09:31.321
in the test production stage?

09:32.489 --> 09:33.991
Why are you standing there?

09:34.074 --> 09:36.451
Get down to the Gwangju factory right now!

09:36.535 --> 09:38.578
Ms. Cha, go to Gwangju.

09:39.162 --> 09:41.581
Get this under control
and get the line back up.

09:42.165 --> 09:43.000
Me?

09:43.083 --> 09:44.626
You want me to go?

09:46.128 --> 09:47.587
If I leave now…

09:50.048 --> 09:51.008
Three hours to get there,

09:51.091 --> 09:53.552
one hour for lunch,
at least two hours to settle things,

09:53.635 --> 09:55.387
and three hours to get back. Nope.

09:56.221 --> 09:57.264
It'll be to late.

09:59.975 --> 10:03.103
People will scatter once it's lunchtime,
so the situation will be over by then.

10:03.937 --> 10:05.272
Even if I head out now…

10:05.814 --> 10:06.940
Okay then,

10:07.649 --> 10:08.734
take the helicopter.

10:09.401 --> 10:12.779
Isn't the helicopter only for executives?

10:12.863 --> 10:15.324
Even regular employees can take it
in an emergency.

10:16.450 --> 10:19.453
Hello, this is Product Planning Team 1
Manager Ko Young-sam.

10:19.536 --> 10:22.456
I'm requesting a helicopter
to go to the Gwangju factory immediately.

10:29.296 --> 10:30.630
Is this really happening?

10:31.423 --> 10:32.674
Fine!

10:32.758 --> 10:35.302
I get to ride a helicopter
and leave work on time.

10:35.385 --> 10:36.636
What a sweet deal.

10:37.012 --> 10:40.140
Huh? Oh, wow.

10:41.558 --> 10:42.434
Awesome.

10:46.146 --> 10:46.980
SAEUM
GWANGJU FACTORY 1

10:47.064 --> 10:49.941
-We won't allow it!
-We can't do it.

10:50.025 --> 10:51.234
We have standards at SAEUM.

10:51.318 --> 10:53.653
How can we put out ice like that
and call it sphere ice?

10:54.529 --> 10:57.699
We did nothing more than produce it

10:57.783 --> 10:59.159
as designed by your team.

10:59.242 --> 11:00.869
It came out fine in the first test.

11:00.952 --> 11:03.330
What, did some sculptor
carve the ice by hand back then?

11:03.413 --> 11:04.790
It comes out fine at first,

11:04.873 --> 11:06.625
but it ends up like that
the more we produce.

11:06.708 --> 11:07.709
What do you expect us to do?

11:07.793 --> 11:08.627
Exactly.

11:08.710 --> 11:11.380
Then let's swap out the parts
and reset the line again!

11:11.463 --> 11:13.799
For crying out loud.
We tried everything already!

11:13.882 --> 11:15.801
No one else is complaining,

11:15.884 --> 11:19.429
so why the heck do you ice people
keep going on like this?

11:20.889 --> 11:21.765
Look who's here.

11:22.682 --> 11:25.268
Oh, Ms. Cha
from the Product Planning Team.

11:26.353 --> 11:27.187
Hi, Ms. Cha.

11:27.270 --> 11:29.106
Hi everyone, how are you all doing?

11:29.189 --> 11:30.107
Hello.

11:30.190 --> 11:31.608
-Hello.
-You got here so fast.

11:31.691 --> 11:33.568
Oh my, look at poor Mr. Kim's face.

11:34.986 --> 11:37.322
Going back and forth between
Seoul and Gwangju must've been a lot.

11:37.406 --> 11:39.116
I'm dying here.

11:39.199 --> 11:40.200
Here.

11:40.283 --> 11:41.952
This is arginine.

11:42.035 --> 11:43.870
They say it does wonders for fatigue.

11:44.788 --> 11:45.997
Make sure you take it, okay?

11:46.873 --> 11:49.000
Did you have a few drinks
again last night?

11:49.084 --> 11:49.960
I went pretty hard.

11:50.043 --> 11:52.712
I tried all sorts of hangover remedies,

11:53.463 --> 11:54.840
and this one was the best.

11:55.590 --> 11:57.300
Just stick to this one, okay?

11:59.302 --> 12:00.762
The clarity really isn't great.

12:03.598 --> 12:05.475
But it's not like we can delay the launch.

12:07.060 --> 12:08.061
Wow, what is this?

12:08.854 --> 12:10.689
Is this some kind of magical orb?

12:11.690 --> 12:14.818
This in a highball
would be absolutely amazing.

12:15.485 --> 12:16.361
See? She likes it.

12:16.445 --> 12:18.738
Well, obviously it's better
than regular ice cubes.

12:18.822 --> 12:20.157
But see? It's not clear enough.

12:20.240 --> 12:22.117
But we can't make it
any clearer than this!

12:22.200 --> 12:25.120
And that's why we should
try changing the equipment!

12:25.203 --> 12:27.831
And how many times
do I have to tell you? We can't!

12:28.623 --> 12:30.709
Okay, okay. In that case,

12:30.792 --> 12:33.462
how about we go ahead
with test production right now

12:33.545 --> 12:37.674
and gradually improve it step by step?

12:37.757 --> 12:40.427
There are lots of other things
we have to test anyway,

12:40.510 --> 12:43.805
like the door opening and closing
and the temperature changes.

12:44.473 --> 12:47.100
We have to make the launch
no matter what, you know?

12:47.767 --> 12:48.935
Isn't that so?

12:49.019 --> 12:50.395
That's exactly what I mean.

12:52.105 --> 12:53.815
Why later and not now?

12:53.899 --> 12:55.150
What was that?

13:05.410 --> 13:07.621
I said, why would you
improve it only after production?

13:15.587 --> 13:17.088
Because if we delay our launch,

13:17.172 --> 13:19.508
our competitor could beat us to market.

13:19.633 --> 13:22.594
And what if that competitor
makes higher quality ice than ours?

13:22.719 --> 13:24.888
We'd still have the first-mover advantage.

13:25.388 --> 13:28.350
We can't afford to fixate
on development and lose on both fronts.

13:28.433 --> 13:31.186
Why not aim to win
on both fronts from the start?

13:31.269 --> 13:33.063
I believe anticipating risks

13:33.772 --> 13:35.524
and thinking about the second-best option

13:35.607 --> 13:37.359
is also an important part of the job.

13:41.029 --> 13:42.656
CHA JI-YOON, SR. ASSOCIATE

13:43.281 --> 13:44.491
"Sr. Associate Cha Ji-yoon."

13:45.951 --> 13:46.785
Yes?

13:46.993 --> 13:48.370
Is this how you work?

13:49.913 --> 13:51.414
What do you mean by that?

13:51.498 --> 13:54.584
A fallback is the last card you play
after doing everything possible.

13:55.627 --> 13:57.379
Preparing a fallback in advance

13:58.380 --> 13:59.339
is not a good attitude.

14:01.341 --> 14:02.926
I don't know who you are,

14:04.177 --> 14:06.846
but you're incredibly idealistic.

14:11.309 --> 14:12.435
I'm Kang Si-woo.

14:14.104 --> 14:15.438
Three-No-Man.

14:15.522 --> 14:16.565
Bloodbath.

14:17.148 --> 14:18.233
Blood.

14:23.405 --> 14:26.616
I heard you were coming back
but didn't expect to see you here.

14:26.700 --> 14:29.160
There's nowhere better than the field
to understand the work.

14:29.244 --> 14:30.745
I just stopped by before returning.

14:30.829 --> 14:32.831
I've heard a lot about you, Mr. Kang.

14:32.914 --> 14:35.083
It's almost lunch,
why don't we eat together?

14:35.166 --> 14:37.752
No, thank you.
I'll just look around a bit and leave.

14:49.806 --> 14:50.640
What do we do now?

14:51.266 --> 14:53.059
Why ask the obvious?
We suspend production.

14:53.852 --> 14:54.769
Ice spikes!

14:56.688 --> 14:57.772
Ice spikes?

14:57.856 --> 14:59.065
You mean reverse icicles?

15:00.108 --> 15:02.986
Yes! Icicles are clear, aren't they?

15:03.069 --> 15:04.988
Maybe we could make it that way.

15:07.157 --> 15:08.908
That's adorable, Ms. Cha.

15:09.534 --> 15:10.619
Well,

15:10.702 --> 15:11.745
work life is so bleak,

15:11.828 --> 15:14.497
at least it's nice that the Planning Team
still has dreamers.

15:14.581 --> 15:15.915
We'll wrap things up here,

15:15.999 --> 15:17.792
you go focus on reporting back.

15:18.293 --> 15:20.879
MANAGER KO YOUNG-SAM

15:21.796 --> 15:23.965
Did word get there already?

15:25.091 --> 15:26.092
Man, I don't want to go back.

15:27.093 --> 15:27.927
I don't want to go.

15:30.930 --> 15:31.806
I'm sorry.

15:31.890 --> 15:34.184
Things got wrapped up
faster than I expected.

15:34.267 --> 15:36.311
The sooner we go, the better. Let's go.

15:36.394 --> 15:37.312
Thank you.

15:43.693 --> 15:45.737
Hold on.
I heard we have another passenger.

15:45.820 --> 15:47.530
-Another passenger?
-Yes.

16:14.432 --> 16:15.975
I'd like to introduce myself properly.

16:16.518 --> 16:19.562
I'm Sr. Associate Cha Ji-yoon
from Product Planning Team 1.

16:20.980 --> 16:23.775
I'm sorry I didn't
recognize you earlier, Mr. Kang.

16:25.777 --> 16:26.736
You've changed a lot.

16:27.696 --> 16:28.530
Pardon?

16:34.786 --> 16:36.121
Weather radar check, clear.

16:37.038 --> 16:38.748
Is everything okay, Captain?

16:38.832 --> 16:40.375
Yes, everything's fine.

16:40.458 --> 16:43.962
It… It's just that we got
an emergency alert this morning.

16:44.045 --> 16:45.672
A heavy… Heavy rain warning.

16:45.755 --> 16:48.591
It's still a while
before it starts pouring down.

16:51.886 --> 16:55.557
You should check
where your life vest is just in case.

16:55.640 --> 16:57.934
Are there any parachutes or something?

16:58.017 --> 16:59.018
Parachutes?

16:59.936 --> 17:01.604
You might start hyperventilating,

17:01.688 --> 17:03.606
so this… Take this and…

17:43.688 --> 17:44.981
I'll let you have this.

17:49.694 --> 17:51.070
Thank y…

17:57.535 --> 18:00.830
I had you flown out
in a helicopter to mediate,

18:01.998 --> 18:04.751
and you shut the whole thing down instead?

18:05.752 --> 18:07.045
What now?

18:08.129 --> 18:08.963
Huh?!

18:10.423 --> 18:11.466
I'm sorry, sir.

18:11.549 --> 18:12.550
I mean…

18:13.676 --> 18:15.011
Am I the only one working here?

18:15.595 --> 18:17.764
Am I the only one getting paid?

18:21.017 --> 18:21.851
People,

18:22.477 --> 18:26.147
come up with a way to contain this mess

18:26.231 --> 18:28.566
and report back by tomorrow morning.

18:29.984 --> 18:31.569
-Got it?
-Yes, sir.

18:32.111 --> 18:32.946
Geez.

18:34.906 --> 18:35.740
Ugh!

18:42.539 --> 18:44.374
Always acting
like he's the only one who works.

18:48.878 --> 18:50.213
Are you okay, Ms. Cha?

18:50.797 --> 18:51.673
Of course, I'm okay.

18:53.550 --> 18:54.509
This isn't anything new.

18:55.593 --> 18:57.929
Let's hurry and go figure out a solution.

19:05.520 --> 19:07.897
RESPONSE PLAN
FOR THE SPHERE ICE REFRIGERATOR SUSPENSION

19:22.495 --> 19:24.289
SPHERE ICE REFRIGERATOR RESPONSE PLAN
FINAL FOR REAL

19:25.290 --> 19:26.416
Time to clock out!

19:27.166 --> 19:28.668
Time to clock out!

19:28.751 --> 19:30.211
Time to clock out!

19:35.383 --> 19:38.011
All right, I'm off.

19:41.014 --> 19:42.181
Of course, Clock-out Fairy.

19:42.765 --> 19:44.267
Did you finish the report?

19:44.350 --> 19:47.270
It's pouring outside,
so don't forget your umbrellas.

19:56.070 --> 19:58.156
Where does Ms. Cha always go

19:58.239 --> 20:00.533
when she leaves right on time
like that every day?

20:00.617 --> 20:01.743
Does she go to the gym?

20:01.826 --> 20:03.369
-Come on.
-Come on.

20:03.453 --> 20:05.330
-Then is it for a date?
-Come on!

20:35.109 --> 20:36.069
That's the stuff.

20:39.364 --> 20:40.198
Hey Buddy,

20:40.949 --> 20:43.868
play some music
for an exhausted office worker.

20:43.952 --> 20:48.247
Way back home, way back home

20:48.331 --> 20:52.126
I'm the happiest when I clock out

20:52.210 --> 20:55.254
Oh beautiful, so beautiful

20:55.338 --> 20:56.297
TURN OFF NOTIFICATIONS

20:56.381 --> 20:57.423
SAEUM 1919

20:57.507 --> 20:58.591
TURN OFF NOTIFICATIONS

20:59.175 --> 21:00.385
Off.

21:01.135 --> 21:02.095
Off.

21:08.267 --> 21:10.103
Is this how you work?

21:10.186 --> 21:13.231
A fallback is the last card you play
after doing everything possible.

21:14.190 --> 21:16.109
Preparing a fallback in advance

21:17.026 --> 21:18.277
is not a good attitude.

21:18.361 --> 21:19.988
What do you want?

21:20.071 --> 21:21.739
That was the best option for me.

21:29.330 --> 21:31.374
Another day of wanting to quit.

21:39.507 --> 21:40.717
RESIGNATION URGE STICKERS

21:45.430 --> 21:46.848
[SAEUM CARD]
PAYMENT DUE: JULY 15

21:48.391 --> 21:49.684
AMOUNT DUE: 1,829,890 WON

21:56.024 --> 21:57.066
I can't quit.

22:00.194 --> 22:01.237
Ugh, never mind!

22:01.612 --> 22:02.447
I'm not quitting.

22:07.910 --> 22:08.745
It's here.

22:14.083 --> 22:15.877
It's not like I don't know
what the best option is.

22:15.960 --> 22:18.713
You look for the second best
because the best doesn't work.

22:19.630 --> 22:22.258
Hey, but still, throwing up

22:23.009 --> 22:24.052
was a bit too much.

22:25.386 --> 22:26.804
Whatever.

22:26.888 --> 22:28.931
Why did he have to ride
the helicopter with me?

22:29.682 --> 22:31.267
That's why they say

22:32.018 --> 22:33.770
you meet your nemesis at work.

22:33.853 --> 22:35.980
Just stay out of his sight and avoid him.

22:37.023 --> 22:39.025
Our company is so huge,

22:39.108 --> 22:42.570
so what are the chances of me
running into a big shot like him again?

22:42.653 --> 22:44.697
Is that why you're having
chicken and beer already?

22:44.781 --> 22:45.740
Hey.

22:46.365 --> 22:49.202
These are the only things
that keep me going.

22:49.285 --> 22:51.954
Hye-ji, now that you're a mom,
how else am I supposed to blow off steam?

22:57.293 --> 22:58.961
I mean, this looks doable.

22:59.879 --> 23:01.005
Why did they say it's not?

23:02.507 --> 23:03.800
Huh? What?

23:04.509 --> 23:05.593
Just something.

23:06.135 --> 23:09.138
Wait, you're not still
pining over Ga-eul, are you?

23:09.222 --> 23:11.182
Why are you bringing up that name?

23:11.265 --> 23:12.975
You scared me.
Why are you getting so worked up?

23:15.394 --> 23:17.730
Great, now you woke Seo-jun.
I'm hanging up.

23:29.742 --> 23:32.745
STANDING EGG - OLD SONG

23:40.878 --> 23:42.004
I hate love.

23:44.382 --> 23:47.051
YEAR 2013

23:48.010 --> 23:50.972
I take another look

23:51.055 --> 23:54.642
Wondering if it's you

23:54.725 --> 23:57.395
I keep turning back

23:57.478 --> 24:00.481
Hoping it's you

24:01.440 --> 24:04.318
Somewhere

24:04.402 --> 24:07.363
Are you listening to the same song?

24:08.072 --> 24:11.284
Could you be standing still too

24:11.367 --> 24:14.120
Thinking of me?

24:22.044 --> 24:22.879
Hi.

24:23.838 --> 24:24.672
Hello.

24:27.216 --> 24:28.801
You're a very good singer.

24:34.849 --> 24:36.475
What instrument do you play?

24:36.559 --> 24:37.351
Sorry?

24:44.066 --> 24:45.026
Drum…

24:48.571 --> 24:49.655
That's so cool.

24:51.741 --> 24:52.575
Here.

24:53.701 --> 24:58.664
"COSMOS" BAND SIGN-UP FORM

25:01.000 --> 25:01.834
Welcome.

25:10.343 --> 25:11.969
The way it gives you

25:12.762 --> 25:15.056
a strange kind of courage
you've never had before.

25:27.860 --> 25:30.613
Just like the song

25:30.696 --> 25:34.033
We used to share a long time ago

25:34.116 --> 25:37.620
That drifted toward me

25:37.703 --> 25:40.706
On the street by chance

25:46.504 --> 25:47.880
The way a brief smile

25:47.964 --> 25:50.508
makes you dream
of a bond that lasts forever.

26:02.561 --> 26:04.063
I'm enlisting next week.

26:06.148 --> 26:07.149
What?

26:07.817 --> 26:08.651
Buy me a meal when I'm out.

26:13.114 --> 26:15.866
The way you don't get tired of waiting
for an answer that never comes.

26:15.950 --> 26:19.328
To Ga-eul's final military leave!

26:19.412 --> 26:20.579
Cheers.

26:22.039 --> 26:23.624
Will you come back to school
as soon as you're out?

26:24.292 --> 26:25.251
I'm going to Australia.

26:25.334 --> 26:28.004
I'm going to make music
in the great outdoors all I want.

26:32.466 --> 26:33.342
That's so cool.

26:35.845 --> 26:37.221
That'll be 10,300 won.

26:37.305 --> 26:41.809
YEAR 2021

26:42.893 --> 26:43.728
These too, please.

26:47.189 --> 26:48.024
Hi.

26:48.607 --> 26:49.483
Ga-eul!

26:50.401 --> 26:51.360
How have you been?

26:52.737 --> 26:56.282
What made me believe
every one of those moments was fate

26:56.365 --> 26:57.199
was love.

27:02.413 --> 27:03.581
I hate love.

27:05.291 --> 27:06.584
It makes too many things

27:07.418 --> 27:08.586
seem possible.

27:21.307 --> 27:22.141
Next.

27:22.516 --> 27:23.684
JEON KEE-TAE
PRODUCT PLANNING TEAM 2

27:29.732 --> 27:30.608
Next.

27:31.233 --> 27:33.277
PARK MI-YOUNG
PRODUCT PLANNING TEAM 2

27:46.665 --> 27:49.418
CHA JI-YOON
PRODUCT PLANNING TEAM 1

27:49.502 --> 27:52.880
CHA JI-YOON
SR. ASSOCIATE

28:03.766 --> 28:06.227
I'm Manager Kang Si-woo,
the new team lead

28:06.310 --> 28:07.645
for Product Planning Team 2.

28:09.688 --> 28:11.899
Why does he have to be
on the team next to mine?

28:16.320 --> 28:17.613
What happened to our team lead?

28:17.696 --> 28:19.865
He's currently on leave
due to health issues.

28:20.533 --> 28:21.909
That came out of nowhere.

28:21.992 --> 28:23.077
He was fine, wasn't he?

28:23.160 --> 28:23.994
I know, right?

28:24.078 --> 28:25.579
Did he have a medical condition?

28:25.663 --> 28:27.081
Let me introduce myself.

28:27.164 --> 28:28.874
I'm Associate Jeon Kee-tae.

28:29.667 --> 28:31.127
Jeon is my last name.

28:31.585 --> 28:32.420
Okay.

28:33.462 --> 28:36.507
Associates Park Mi-young, Kim Yeong-jin,
Han Jae-rim, Kim Seung-ji,

28:36.590 --> 28:37.883
and Jeon Kee-tae.

28:37.967 --> 28:39.677
Sr. Associates
Choi Jung-in, Park In-cheol.

28:39.760 --> 28:42.513
I know all of your names and titles,
so no need to tell me.

28:43.764 --> 28:46.142
I'll be communicating with you
via messages from now on.

28:47.268 --> 28:49.145
Report your work to me by email.

28:49.228 --> 28:52.898
Now, please start by putting together
a list of your current tasks

28:52.982 --> 28:54.150
and sending it to me.

28:56.318 --> 28:59.905
Should we all go out for lunch
as a welcome meal

28:59.989 --> 29:01.991
for you, Mr. Kang?

29:02.074 --> 29:05.119
I'll eat on my own
after checking your emails.

29:05.202 --> 29:06.328
All right, then.

29:15.129 --> 29:16.213
Good luck.

29:30.186 --> 29:32.813
That means he wants everyone
to finish before lunch, right?

29:32.897 --> 29:34.315
It means they shouldn't even

29:34.398 --> 29:36.734
think about having lunch
unless they finish.

29:37.943 --> 29:40.279
You think Mr. Ko is better
compared to Three-No-Man?

29:40.362 --> 29:42.156
You mean, choose who's the worst

29:42.781 --> 29:43.741
and the second worst?

29:46.118 --> 29:47.328
Mr. Ko's coming.

29:57.755 --> 29:59.840
In and out, and in and out.

29:59.924 --> 30:02.551
What is this, an office or a temple?

30:03.802 --> 30:05.804
Let me look at your reports.

30:11.644 --> 30:12.603
RESPONSE PLAN

30:16.607 --> 30:19.777
You've been a Sr. Associate for that long,
and you bring me this?

30:19.860 --> 30:21.403
You want to be a Sr. Associate forever?

30:22.112 --> 30:22.988
I'm sorry, sir.

30:26.158 --> 30:28.619
That new team lead
won't give you advice like this.

30:28.702 --> 30:30.371
He'll be busy looking out for himself

30:30.454 --> 30:32.706
no matter what happens to his people.

30:42.174 --> 30:43.300
Thank you.

30:44.510 --> 30:46.637
I wish I could tell myself
from five years ago

30:46.720 --> 30:48.806
to write your cover letter
and run somewhere else.

30:51.350 --> 30:53.978
I wish I could tell myself
from when I was your age to learn

30:54.061 --> 30:55.396
from someone
who's smart and competent,

30:55.479 --> 30:58.691
instead of working under a boss
who just dumps work on you

30:58.774 --> 31:00.859
while sucking up to the higher-ups.

31:01.360 --> 31:03.195
You can do that now, can't you?

31:03.279 --> 31:04.154
It's too late for me.

31:04.238 --> 31:07.199
I'm already used to a boss
who only does the bare minimum.

31:08.117 --> 31:10.077
Is this the so-called seven-year slump?

31:12.955 --> 31:14.832
LADY NAM

31:15.791 --> 31:16.625
Hey, Mom.

31:16.709 --> 31:17.876
You haven't eaten yet, right?

31:18.877 --> 31:20.004
I was just about to eat.

31:20.087 --> 31:21.630
I'm by your office, so just come out.

31:21.714 --> 31:22.840
I'll send you directions.

31:22.923 --> 31:24.049
Mom.

31:24.133 --> 31:25.050
Mom?

31:38.188 --> 31:40.065
SLOW POKE

31:50.576 --> 31:51.660
Ms. Cha Ji-yoon?

31:53.370 --> 31:54.246
That's me.

31:55.164 --> 31:56.248
And you are?

31:56.957 --> 31:58.083
Hello.

31:58.167 --> 32:00.544
I'm Lee Jeong-woo. I'm here to meet you.

32:01.170 --> 32:02.004
Pardon?

32:07.343 --> 32:08.636
Just a moment, please.

32:22.691 --> 32:24.068
Come on, pick up.

32:38.207 --> 32:39.375
Can I go in?

33:02.314 --> 33:05.609
If your fridge or washing machine breaks,
do you fix them yourself?

33:07.069 --> 33:08.195
No, I call for service.

33:08.821 --> 33:10.155
What about computers?

33:10.239 --> 33:13.367
My friends who were engineering majors
usually build their own.

33:14.576 --> 33:16.161
There are good all-in-ones these days.

33:18.163 --> 33:20.666
Still, it's pretty incredible
that you work

33:20.749 --> 33:22.084
at an electronics company.

33:23.043 --> 33:24.545
My mom totally freaks out

33:24.628 --> 33:26.547
when the circuit breaker trips.

33:27.423 --> 33:28.799
My sister once called someone

33:29.383 --> 33:31.301
just because a light bulb went out…

33:33.387 --> 33:35.305
and got into a huge fight
with her husband.

33:35.931 --> 33:38.225
Running into someone
from work is bad enough,

33:39.143 --> 33:40.936
so why did it have to be Three-No-Man?

33:41.562 --> 33:42.771
Oh, Ji-yoon,

33:43.397 --> 33:44.898
you've got some sauce on your face.

33:46.442 --> 33:47.985
No, the other side.

34:10.048 --> 34:12.718
I should tell you
before this gets any more awkward.

34:12.801 --> 34:13.969
Tell me what?

34:14.052 --> 34:17.431
I'm in a temporary no-dating phase.

34:20.058 --> 34:20.893
Oh, right.

34:22.311 --> 34:25.063
I haven't completely ended things

34:25.689 --> 34:27.900
with my ex-boyfriend yet.

34:30.360 --> 34:31.695
I'm so sorry

34:32.529 --> 34:34.323
for wasting your time like this.

34:37.201 --> 34:38.535
So…

34:40.704 --> 34:41.663
I'll pay

34:43.582 --> 34:44.833
for your lunch.

34:47.795 --> 34:49.421
This caller is unavailable.

34:49.505 --> 34:50.589
Not answering, huh?

34:51.965 --> 34:53.801
I swear, I'm going to disown her.

34:56.345 --> 34:57.429
Hey, Ms. Choi!

34:58.055 --> 35:00.015
Ji-yoon! Have you been well?

35:00.098 --> 35:00.933
Yes.

35:01.517 --> 35:02.935
I saw you won
the Design of the Year award.

35:03.018 --> 35:04.144
Congratulations.

35:04.228 --> 35:05.145
Thank you.

35:07.648 --> 35:10.025
Would you like to come
for some food, if you have time?

35:12.319 --> 35:13.153
Are you perhaps…

35:13.237 --> 35:14.863
She's getting married.

35:15.489 --> 35:17.991
Congratulations!
Of course, I'll be at your wedding.

35:18.075 --> 35:19.117
No pressure, though.

35:19.785 --> 35:21.620
-Okay.
-See you later.

35:21.703 --> 35:22.996
Shall we head out?

35:23.080 --> 35:24.498
-Bye!
-Take care.

35:26.333 --> 35:28.001
I'm so jealous of the Design Team

35:28.085 --> 35:30.295
that they get to work
with a cool boss like her.

35:30.379 --> 35:31.213
Tell me about it.

35:31.296 --> 35:34.007
She's talented,
straightforward, and funny.

35:34.508 --> 35:37.427
She's my greatest mentor and role model.

35:40.097 --> 35:41.682
I need to book a wedding venue too.

35:42.766 --> 35:43.934
I hear your boyfriend is very sweet.

35:44.560 --> 35:45.769
I'm so jealous!

35:45.853 --> 35:46.687
Sorry?

35:50.023 --> 35:52.651
Boyfriend? What is she on about?

35:52.776 --> 35:53.735
Ms. Cha.

35:55.153 --> 35:57.322
-I heard you're getting married soon.
-No, I'm not.

35:57.406 --> 35:59.700
Come on, don't be so shy.

35:59.783 --> 36:00.826
Congratulations.

36:01.368 --> 36:02.327
Wait.

36:04.329 --> 36:06.081
Ms. Cha, what's happening?

36:06.164 --> 36:07.666
I don't know.

36:08.917 --> 36:10.085
Maybe there's a fake rumor.

36:12.754 --> 36:16.091
Well, well. I heard lunch blind dates
are all the rage these days,

36:16.174 --> 36:18.385
but I had no idea
our dear colleague was this trendy.

36:18.468 --> 36:20.721
Was it sparks at first sight,
all fireworks?

36:21.471 --> 36:23.223
Did you just come back from a blind date?

36:23.307 --> 36:24.975
-No-ah, go on in first.
-Wait!

36:25.058 --> 36:26.018
-Quiet.
-Why?

36:26.602 --> 36:27.936
-Isn't it true?
-Wait, a blind date…

36:28.478 --> 36:29.354
Don't go, No-ah.

36:31.773 --> 36:33.901
What the hell?
Who said I went on a blind date?

36:33.984 --> 36:35.444
I saw it on the online forum.

36:35.527 --> 36:38.739
Here. See?
The forum's blowing up right now.

36:42.200 --> 36:44.745
Looks like Planning Team 1's
Sr. Associate "C" will get married soon.

36:44.828 --> 36:47.706
Heard someone saw her on a blind date
at a poke place during lunch.

36:47.789 --> 36:49.917
The man stroked her face and everything.

36:50.000 --> 36:51.209
-Wait.
-Really?

36:51.293 --> 36:53.587
So, the Clock-out Fairy
doesn't even waste lunchtime.

36:53.670 --> 36:54.671
Is she a Blind-Date Fairy now?

36:54.755 --> 36:56.465
-Hahaha.
-Wonder if it went well.

36:58.300 --> 36:59.134
Hang on.

37:05.307 --> 37:06.183
"Hang on"?

37:17.778 --> 37:19.863
Hey, is it fake news?

37:21.323 --> 37:22.157
Is it raining?

37:22.240 --> 37:25.035
He spread a rumor
in that short amount of time?

37:25.994 --> 37:27.496
I didn't think he'd do such a thing.

37:27.996 --> 37:29.873
Who did the "No People"
Three-No-Man even tell?

37:31.124 --> 37:33.418
But he's the only one
who saw the guy touch my face.

37:46.056 --> 37:47.474
Did you enjoy your lunch?

37:48.183 --> 37:49.059
Yes.

37:55.399 --> 37:56.358
By any chance,

37:57.150 --> 37:59.194
did you hear the rumor

37:59.820 --> 38:01.405
that I was on a blind date at lunch?

38:02.197 --> 38:03.490
Was that a blind date?

38:04.074 --> 38:07.160
I went on the date against my will,
but I won't ever see him again.

38:07.244 --> 38:08.870
Why would someone spread

38:08.954 --> 38:12.207
a rumor like that
when they don't know the full story?

38:13.625 --> 38:15.293
You expect me to know the answer?

38:16.503 --> 38:17.462
It wasn't him.

38:18.547 --> 38:20.507
There's a lot of fake news
around the office.

38:21.216 --> 38:22.342
Just letting you know.

38:29.057 --> 38:30.684
JULY 26
PARK HYEONG-JIN AND CHOI SOO-JIN

38:31.852 --> 38:35.063
Manager Choi Soo-jin
from the Design Team is getting married.

38:35.147 --> 38:36.815
Are you going to the wedding?

38:43.989 --> 38:45.824
Don't you think you should go?

38:45.907 --> 38:49.745
The Planning Team and Design Team
work together a lot.

38:52.414 --> 38:53.915
Why would I go there?

39:04.926 --> 39:07.137
What's his problem?

39:14.102 --> 39:16.813
Why would you send a man
right where my office is?

39:16.897 --> 39:19.357
Do you know
what kind of humiliation I went through?

39:19.441 --> 39:21.610
I wouldn't have done it
if you were doing well yourself.

39:21.693 --> 39:23.236
What am I not doing well?

39:23.320 --> 39:25.280
Why ask the obvious? Getting married.

39:25.864 --> 39:28.700
Who even gets married
at my age these days?

39:28.784 --> 39:31.703
If you weren't going to marry,
why did you live with--

39:32.329 --> 39:33.538
Live with?

39:33.622 --> 39:34.998
What are you on about?

39:35.082 --> 39:36.792
I didn't say anything!

39:38.794 --> 39:39.669
You brat.

39:40.253 --> 39:42.214
You give back every cent I sent you.

39:43.590 --> 39:44.508
Fine.

39:45.175 --> 39:47.385
I never saw it myself
and you were never caught,

39:47.469 --> 39:49.429
so that means nothing happened, right?

39:50.013 --> 39:51.848
It did happen.
What do you mean nothing happened?

39:51.932 --> 39:54.601
Yes, I lived with Ga-eul

39:54.684 --> 39:57.104
and even thought about getting married,
but we broke up. So what?

39:57.187 --> 40:00.690
Exactly, so now go meet a decent guy
and get married already!

40:00.774 --> 40:01.650
No!

40:02.234 --> 40:03.777
Seriously.

40:07.072 --> 40:07.906
Did you

40:09.407 --> 40:11.159
take money from your sister too?

40:11.243 --> 40:13.036
I was just trying to be a peacekeeper.

40:13.120 --> 40:14.037
You little!

40:14.121 --> 40:16.957
I can forgive cohabitation,
but I won't forgive two-timing, you punk!

40:19.126 --> 40:20.418
I'm home.

40:20.502 --> 40:21.795
The hamburger?

40:24.005 --> 40:25.048
Here.

40:26.758 --> 40:28.552
Stop eating junk like this.

40:36.476 --> 40:37.477
Did you pull an all-nighter?

40:38.728 --> 40:39.688
Yeah.

40:40.939 --> 40:43.358
So why would you quit your job

40:43.441 --> 40:45.026
to write some web novel?

40:45.110 --> 40:46.736
If you want to, write a fantasy novel.

40:47.320 --> 40:48.613
Office Proposal?

40:49.156 --> 40:50.866
Who would read about coworkers dating?

40:51.491 --> 40:53.994
Why are you nagging me again
the second you walk in?

40:54.077 --> 40:57.205
You need to get it together
and start dating again and all that.

40:59.082 --> 41:01.626
So why date a jerk like that
just to break off your engagement?

41:11.344 --> 41:12.470
GOO-WON

41:12.554 --> 41:13.889
Babe, did you have dinner?

41:13.972 --> 41:15.807
Where should we go this weekend?

41:17.017 --> 41:18.351
I guess he's swamped.

41:22.355 --> 41:24.191
I just sent you an email,

41:24.274 --> 41:26.276
so pull up the response plan
from the attachment.

41:27.861 --> 41:28.945
This last minute?

41:32.991 --> 41:35.911
I heard even the test production stopped
because of this clarity issue.

41:35.994 --> 41:36.828
So, Mr. Ko,

41:36.912 --> 41:39.956
what will happen
if this situation drags on?

41:40.040 --> 41:42.542
That's why I've prepared a response plan.

41:44.211 --> 41:45.212
Ms. Cha.

41:45.295 --> 41:46.338
Yes.

41:51.218 --> 41:53.220
I propose we launch
in North America first

41:53.887 --> 41:56.556
if the domestic launch gets stalled.

41:56.640 --> 41:59.351
Wait. This is mine.

42:01.811 --> 42:04.397
None of these are good enough.

42:06.358 --> 42:08.235
I'll handle this report myself.

42:08.318 --> 42:10.028
Send all your reports to me by email.

42:10.111 --> 42:11.029
NORTH AMERICAN MARKET SURVEY
ON SPHERE ICE

42:11.112 --> 42:12.113
Yes, sir.

42:13.490 --> 42:17.911
Our market research shows that demand
for sphere ice is higher in North America

42:17.994 --> 42:19.454
than the domestic market,

42:19.537 --> 42:24.209
so the consumers there care more
about the shape and function than clarity.

42:24.292 --> 42:25.543
So,

42:25.627 --> 42:28.046
we should target overseas markets first,

42:28.129 --> 42:31.007
then use that success
to build momentum for the domestic laun--

42:32.133 --> 42:33.343
404 NOT FOUND

42:38.598 --> 42:39.808
Well, uh…

42:39.891 --> 42:42.602
Domestic launch…

42:43.436 --> 42:44.813
What are you doing, Ms. Cha?

42:44.896 --> 42:45.939
I apologize.

42:46.022 --> 42:47.941
There's been an error. Let me reboot it.

42:50.402 --> 42:52.779
Mr. Ko. Please continue.

42:52.862 --> 42:54.155
Right. Of course.

42:54.239 --> 42:57.450
Well, if we launch overseas…
I mean in North America,

42:57.534 --> 42:59.619
we'll break into that market, and then…

43:01.830 --> 43:04.749
I think it'd be better for me
to explain with some visual aid.

43:04.833 --> 43:07.043
Then let me ask you a question
in the meantime.

43:08.837 --> 43:09.671
Sure.

43:09.754 --> 43:11.131
What is sphere ice?

43:13.174 --> 43:15.010
You just came from the US.

43:15.760 --> 43:18.263
Haven't you been
to a whiskey bar, Mr. Kang?

43:18.346 --> 43:21.433
Sphere ice is an ice ball
shaped like an orb.

43:21.516 --> 43:22.392
No, not that.

43:23.184 --> 43:26.146
I'm asking you about its qualities,
not its shape.

43:26.229 --> 43:28.440
It melts more slowly
than regular ice cubes,

43:28.523 --> 43:32.694
so it lets you enjoy
the drink's original flavor for longer.

43:33.320 --> 43:36.281
Couldn't you just use an ice mold
already on the market for that?

43:36.364 --> 43:39.534
A sphere-ice refrigerator is more costly
than a regular one.

43:40.243 --> 43:41.244
Why should one buy it then?

43:42.829 --> 43:44.122
Well…

43:44.205 --> 43:45.206
In that case,

43:45.290 --> 43:48.752
what do you think
is the core value of sphere ice, Mr. Kang?

43:49.377 --> 43:50.587
Its aesthetics.

43:52.297 --> 43:54.549
People pay more to buy luxury bags

43:54.632 --> 43:57.552
not because of function,
but because of their rarity and design.

43:58.053 --> 44:00.764
The sphere ice our refrigerator makes
has to be like that.

44:00.847 --> 44:03.183
Not some rough imitation of an ice chunk,

44:03.266 --> 44:07.479
but a clear and perfect luxury product
made possible by innovative technology.

44:07.562 --> 44:09.856
As I explained earlier,

44:09.939 --> 44:11.816
that's not possible
with current technology, so…

44:11.900 --> 44:13.526
Do you think so too, Ms. Cha?

44:14.319 --> 44:15.278
Pardon?

44:15.362 --> 44:18.281
Is there really no other way
to make the ice clearer?

44:23.828 --> 44:25.038
Ice spikes!

44:25.747 --> 44:27.374
Icicles are clear, aren’t they?

44:27.999 --> 44:29.751
Maybe we could make it that way.

44:41.054 --> 44:42.055
There isn't.

44:45.683 --> 44:46.851
So then,

44:46.935 --> 44:49.396
what's your verdict, Mr. Kang?

44:49.479 --> 44:51.648
The sphere ice refrigerator launch plan

44:52.232 --> 44:53.817
should be suspended entirely.

44:59.656 --> 45:01.324
We've already come this far.

45:01.408 --> 45:04.244
Stopping so suddenly seems just…

45:05.370 --> 45:08.581
If we stop now,
we'll have to absorb enormous losses.

45:09.374 --> 45:11.209
That's an irresponsible thing to say.

45:11.292 --> 45:14.838
The losses will be less than the cost
of launching a flawed product.

45:30.437 --> 45:33.565
Stealing your own subordinate's report?

45:33.648 --> 45:35.692
Way to hit a new low, you shameless boss!

45:38.736 --> 45:39.571
You know what?

45:39.654 --> 45:41.781
If the pay's the same,

45:41.865 --> 45:43.741
better a salary thief
than a corporate slave.

45:45.118 --> 45:46.619
I'll do just that.

45:47.287 --> 45:49.247
Is this the model
that was presented at CES?

45:49.330 --> 45:51.040
CES: A GLOBAL ELECTRONICS TRADE SHOW
FOR UNVEILING NEW PRODUCTS

45:51.124 --> 45:51.958
Yes.

45:53.585 --> 45:54.919
Why didn't you tell them?

45:56.171 --> 45:57.005
Sorry?

45:57.297 --> 45:58.381
About ice spikes.

46:01.301 --> 46:04.053
Did you think it'd just get shot down
like at the factory

46:04.679 --> 46:06.514
or you'd get your idea stolen like today?

46:08.224 --> 46:10.935
Is that why you didn't say anything
when I gave you the chance?

46:17.025 --> 46:17.984
JEON KEE-TAE KEE-TAE

46:20.153 --> 46:21.029
Hey.

46:23.072 --> 46:24.240
I'm on my way.

46:38.463 --> 46:39.672
It's not that I didn't,

46:40.715 --> 46:42.300
I just couldn't say it yet.

46:43.218 --> 46:46.137
Because I'm not completely sure
about it right now.

47:23.383 --> 47:24.509
I'm here.

47:24.592 --> 47:25.510
Hey.

47:27.262 --> 47:29.013
This is our team's cash gift
for the wedding.

47:29.097 --> 47:30.056
Pass it along for us.

47:30.139 --> 47:31.349
Aren't you going?

47:31.432 --> 47:33.685
I took charge
and collected everyone's money,

47:33.768 --> 47:35.353
but my mother-in-law's coming.

47:35.436 --> 47:36.396
All right, then.

47:36.479 --> 47:39.065
I'm going to be there anyway,
might as well have a full pocket.

47:39.148 --> 47:39.983
Thanks.

47:41.276 --> 47:42.569
Can I just ask one more favor?

47:42.652 --> 47:43.611
What is it?

47:44.195 --> 47:47.323
I know you're the Clock-out Fairy,
but we need one more person's.

47:47.407 --> 47:50.159
Dear Fairy, could you stay for a bit
and get Mr. Kang's cash gift too?

47:50.243 --> 47:51.536
No way!

47:51.619 --> 47:52.954
Mr. Kang makes me uncomfortable.

47:53.037 --> 47:55.081
Me too,
but my mother-in-law is even worse.

47:55.164 --> 47:57.333
I'm going nuts. I can't.
I'm leaving. You're the best!

47:57.417 --> 47:58.251
Hey!

47:58.334 --> 47:59.168
Hey!

48:00.169 --> 48:01.087
Geez.

48:04.090 --> 48:04.966
JEON KEE-TAE
SAEUM

48:34.537 --> 48:35.830
Why would I go there?

48:58.311 --> 49:01.147
He snapped at me
just for asking if he was going to go.

49:03.900 --> 49:05.860
So how could I ask him for a cash gift?

49:10.782 --> 49:12.450
The bus arriving soon

49:12.533 --> 49:16.204
is number 266.

49:40.728 --> 49:43.773
Where did you find this?

49:43.856 --> 49:45.775
I found it in the product showroom.

49:48.611 --> 49:49.779
Thank you.

49:51.280 --> 49:53.449
Did you come
all the way here just for this?

49:53.533 --> 49:55.785
Well, you could say that.

49:57.078 --> 49:58.496
You could've given it to me later.

50:02.500 --> 50:03.501
Thank you.

50:04.085 --> 50:04.919
Well, then…

50:05.461 --> 50:06.504
Have a good night.

50:11.134 --> 50:12.093
Hello.

50:27.358 --> 50:29.569
What? Why is he getting on this bus?

50:33.948 --> 50:35.491
What? No!

50:43.708 --> 50:45.334
There are plenty of other seats.

50:45.835 --> 50:47.128
Why sit right next to me?

50:48.963 --> 50:51.424
Is he following me or something?

50:52.133 --> 50:52.967
Why?

51:00.850 --> 51:02.935
I saw a lot of interesting stuff
in your notebook.

51:05.438 --> 51:07.190
Wait, you read my notebook?

51:08.107 --> 51:09.609
I had to find its owner.

51:11.736 --> 51:13.529
There were a lot of good ideas in there.

51:14.155 --> 51:15.323
If it were up to me,

51:16.783 --> 51:19.327
I'd have given you
about ten of those stamps.

51:19.410 --> 51:20.411
GREAT JOB!

51:20.495 --> 51:22.205
And one more if that's not enough.

51:28.002 --> 51:29.796
Thank you?

51:31.005 --> 51:33.883
Wait, I didn't mean I want one more stamp.

51:37.094 --> 51:39.889
He came all the way after me
to give me my notebook back,

51:39.972 --> 51:41.724
and now he's complimenting my ideas?

51:43.684 --> 51:44.644
Could it be?

51:48.189 --> 51:50.107
I'll make sure it gets delivered safely.

51:50.983 --> 51:52.568
And what am I supposed to give you?

51:52.652 --> 51:55.112
Wedding gift money for Ms. Choi Soo-jin.

51:55.196 --> 51:57.865
Weren't you an engineering major, Ms. Cha?

51:58.449 --> 52:00.034
That's right, engineering.

52:00.117 --> 52:02.870
I think you would've been
good at something more creative.

52:06.999 --> 52:08.417
Would you prefer bank transfer?

52:08.501 --> 52:10.086
Should I give you my bank details?

52:10.670 --> 52:13.297
Ms. Cha, would you give a cash gift

52:13.381 --> 52:14.757
for your ex-husband's wedding?

52:15.341 --> 52:16.467
Sorry?

52:17.426 --> 52:21.722
This stop is Wonam-dong.

52:21.806 --> 52:25.601
The next stop is Korea Corporation.

52:43.911 --> 52:45.496
Mr. Kang is…

52:46.330 --> 52:47.540
Ms. Choi's

52:48.207 --> 52:49.417
ex-husband?

53:02.513 --> 53:04.223
-Ready for the picture?
-Come here.

53:04.307 --> 53:06.267
One, two, three.

53:06.976 --> 53:08.519
-Let's do one more.
-Okay.

53:09.186 --> 53:10.396
One, two, three.

53:11.772 --> 53:13.357
-Congratulations.
-Stay for the food later.

53:13.441 --> 53:14.901
There's no way.

53:15.526 --> 53:17.486
Why would Ms. Choi do that?

53:17.570 --> 53:19.322
-You look so beautiful!
-Thank you.

53:19.405 --> 53:20.656
Why on earth?

53:21.157 --> 53:22.450
JULY 26
PARK HYEONG-JIN AND CHOI-SOO JIN

53:22.533 --> 53:24.368
Don't you think you should go?

53:26.120 --> 53:27.330
Why would I go there?

53:27.413 --> 53:30.374
Ms. Cha, would you give a cash gift

53:30.458 --> 53:31.792
for your ex-husband's wedding?

53:48.809 --> 53:50.353
This is Cha Ji-yoon.

53:50.436 --> 53:52.229
I wanted to apologize, Mr. Kang.

53:52.313 --> 53:54.815
I made a mistake
because I didn't know better.

53:55.900 --> 53:59.028
I'm sorry if I offended you.

53:59.862 --> 54:03.616
MANAGER KANG SI-WOO

54:45.241 --> 54:49.036
Some people say marriage
is where romance goes to die.

54:50.246 --> 54:51.205
But back then,

54:52.123 --> 54:53.165
I believed…

54:55.167 --> 54:57.003
that marriage was where romance

54:57.086 --> 54:58.462
was made complete.

55:07.680 --> 55:08.806
HAWAII

55:13.060 --> 55:14.270
I've made up my mind.

55:15.563 --> 55:17.648
My honeymoon will be in Hawaii!

55:19.650 --> 55:21.485
But don't you need to be married
to go on a honeymoon?

55:21.569 --> 55:23.112
Of course.

55:27.199 --> 55:28.534
Let's just go now.

55:28.617 --> 55:29.493
What?

55:31.120 --> 55:34.623
If we go now,
plumeria will be in full bloom.

55:34.707 --> 55:36.375
We can breathe in that scent

55:36.459 --> 55:38.919
while you swim and I make music.

55:39.462 --> 55:42.256
What do you think?
Doesn't that sound super exciting?

55:42.339 --> 55:43.299
Yes, it does.

55:43.924 --> 55:45.801
That's why I'm saving it.

55:46.385 --> 55:47.553
What?

55:47.636 --> 55:49.263
-Let's just go.
-No.

55:49.346 --> 55:50.639
-Come on, now.
-Stop it.

55:50.723 --> 55:52.767
-Let's just go! Come on!
-Stop it!

55:52.850 --> 55:54.852
-Let's just go!
-Stop that!

55:54.935 --> 55:56.062
-Let's go!
-Stop.

55:56.145 --> 55:58.022
Huh? Let's go!

56:17.917 --> 56:20.628
I'm going to see the winter sea.
I'll come back with a killer song.

56:21.420 --> 56:22.296
Love you.

56:27.968 --> 56:30.930
I loved your free spirit.

56:34.517 --> 56:38.104
But in the end,
that became the reason why we broke up.

56:55.329 --> 56:56.872
WHY AREN'T YOU HERE?

56:56.956 --> 56:58.582
WHERE ARE YOU?
WHEN ARE YOU COMING BACK?

56:58.666 --> 57:00.459
I'M WORRIED SO CALL ME
PICK UP YOUR PHONE!

57:00.543 --> 57:03.587
OKAY, LET'S END IT HERE… IT'S OVER

57:19.061 --> 57:21.272
If you're sorry,
buy me a drink or something.

57:23.691 --> 57:26.026
The most important variables in life

57:26.652 --> 57:27.570
often appear

57:28.362 --> 57:30.406
when you least expect them.

57:42.126 --> 57:43.085
Yes, Mr. Kang.

57:43.919 --> 57:45.838
-You see me, right?
-Sorry?

57:46.797 --> 57:48.007
Where are you?

57:48.090 --> 57:49.383
Right across the street.

57:54.096 --> 57:55.097
Which side?

58:19.371 --> 58:21.332
You can't just stop there like that.

58:29.215 --> 58:30.341
Let's go.

58:34.470 --> 58:35.679
Who would've imagined

58:36.263 --> 58:39.391
I'd be meeting this guy
alone on a weekend?

58:40.726 --> 58:42.269
Was he always that tall?

58:57.451 --> 58:59.245
I'm surprised you know a place like this.

58:59.828 --> 59:01.997
-My friend owns the place.
-Welcome to--

59:02.081 --> 59:04.625
What? When did you get back from the US?

59:05.501 --> 59:06.919
He gives me free stuff.

59:07.503 --> 59:09.505
He has a friend?

59:09.588 --> 59:12.174
If it's this empty,
shouldn't you just shut down the place?

59:12.258 --> 59:14.343
You little punk,
first thing you do is nagging?

59:14.426 --> 59:16.053
Oh, please take a seat here.

59:16.136 --> 59:17.096
Oh, okay.

59:18.764 --> 59:20.557
And he's normal.

59:28.774 --> 59:30.276
Are you okay with single malt?

59:30.359 --> 59:31.568
Yes, anything is fine.

59:33.570 --> 59:35.698
What's with this gentle tone?

59:43.372 --> 59:45.833
Let me run to the storeroom real quick.

59:56.760 --> 59:59.555
He's like a completely different person
outside the office.

01:00:00.806 --> 01:00:02.474
I bet you were surprised to hear from me.

01:00:03.517 --> 01:00:05.311
Yes, a little.

01:00:07.688 --> 01:00:09.106
But why did you…

01:00:10.399 --> 01:00:12.026
Did the wedding go well?

01:00:12.860 --> 01:00:15.112
So that's what he wanted to see me for.

01:00:15.195 --> 01:00:16.030
Yes.

01:00:16.613 --> 01:00:17.448
How was it?

01:00:24.330 --> 01:00:26.123
It was normal…

01:00:27.791 --> 01:00:28.751
and happy.

01:00:31.420 --> 01:00:32.963
What am I saying?

01:00:38.218 --> 01:00:40.429
The food wasn't great, though.

01:00:45.434 --> 01:00:47.186
What did you do today, Mr. Kang?

01:00:47.853 --> 01:00:49.646
I worked out all day.

01:00:49.730 --> 01:00:50.564
Of course,

01:00:50.647 --> 01:00:53.650
the best thing to do on a day like today
is to keep yourself busy

01:00:53.734 --> 01:00:56.653
and drown yourself in alcohol…

01:01:00.949 --> 01:01:01.784
Right.

01:01:01.867 --> 01:01:04.453
I guess I should drink quite a bit today.

01:01:16.590 --> 01:01:20.302
I'm no longer the team lead
for Product Planning Team 2.

01:01:21.178 --> 01:01:22.221
Pardon?

01:01:23.180 --> 01:01:24.264
I got fired.

01:01:31.021 --> 01:01:33.982
That's exactly why
you shouldn't have suggested

01:01:34.066 --> 01:01:37.486
suspending the whole thing.

01:01:48.914 --> 01:01:49.957
PRESIDENT HAN U-JIN

01:01:51.208 --> 01:01:52.084
It's the President.

01:01:52.543 --> 01:01:53.877
You go on and drink.

01:01:54.503 --> 01:01:56.046
This might take a while.

01:01:56.130 --> 01:01:58.799
Yes. Don't worry about me.
Please take your time.

01:02:00.634 --> 01:02:01.468
Mr. Kang!

01:02:03.387 --> 01:02:06.557
Just apologize and beg like you mean it.

01:02:07.099 --> 01:02:08.308
Good luck.

01:02:12.646 --> 01:02:13.856
This is Kang Si-woo.

01:02:16.358 --> 01:02:17.901
He really needs to soften his edges.

01:02:22.114 --> 01:02:23.157
Would you like a refill?

01:02:23.240 --> 01:02:24.116
Please.

01:02:27.953 --> 01:02:29.079
Actually,

01:02:29.163 --> 01:02:30.622
fill it up.

01:02:30.998 --> 01:02:32.166
All right, fill it up.

01:02:33.250 --> 01:02:34.334
Got it.

01:02:44.136 --> 01:02:48.056
OKAY, LET'S END IT HERE… IT'S OVER

01:02:49.391 --> 01:02:50.851
When you think about it,

01:02:52.519 --> 01:02:53.687
I actually…

01:02:56.356 --> 01:03:00.319
got fired by Cho Ga-eul, right?

01:03:05.574 --> 01:03:07.618
I can't even move on
to another person like this.

01:03:15.042 --> 01:03:17.586
OKAY, LET'S END IT HERE… IT'S OVER
DELIVERED

01:03:18.462 --> 01:03:19.296
Yes.

01:03:19.379 --> 01:03:22.466
I'll make sure the handover
is completed by next week.

01:03:23.842 --> 01:03:24.676
Okay.

01:03:27.429 --> 01:03:29.681
PRESIDENT HAN U-JIN

01:03:42.277 --> 01:03:43.153
What happened?

01:03:43.237 --> 01:03:45.113
She went crazy as soon as you stepped out.

01:03:46.949 --> 01:03:48.283
I picked the wrong day.

01:03:49.660 --> 01:03:50.953
Come on, get up.

01:03:51.036 --> 01:03:52.162
I'll take you home.

01:03:55.082 --> 01:03:56.208
Excuse me, ma'am?

01:04:01.421 --> 01:04:02.256
What should we do?

01:04:08.679 --> 01:04:09.721
Ms. Cha Ji-yoon.

01:04:09.805 --> 01:04:10.681
Yeah?

01:04:11.890 --> 01:04:12.933
You're late.

01:04:19.231 --> 01:04:22.568
I'm never ever late, you know.

01:04:23.527 --> 01:04:25.153
I may not look it,

01:04:25.237 --> 01:04:27.864
but I'm actually the Clock-in

01:04:27.948 --> 01:04:29.449
and Clock-out fairy.

01:04:31.410 --> 01:04:33.245
A fairy, you say?

01:04:34.580 --> 01:04:36.081
How long have you been a fairy?

01:04:37.916 --> 01:04:40.711
Up until my third year of working,

01:04:41.378 --> 01:04:43.422
I pulled all-nighters like it was nothing.

01:04:43.505 --> 01:04:47.593
I really had so much
I wanted to do back then.

01:04:48.510 --> 01:04:51.972
That's when you're full of passion
but short on know-how.

01:04:52.055 --> 01:04:53.348
Exactly.

01:04:53.432 --> 01:04:55.976
Then around my fifth year,

01:04:56.560 --> 01:04:58.937
I got so busy handling work
dumped down from the higher-ups

01:04:59.021 --> 01:05:00.856
and cleaning up after my subordinates

01:05:00.939 --> 01:05:04.026
that not even ten of me
would've been enough.

01:05:04.985 --> 01:05:08.113
Which is also why that's
when people switch jobs the most.

01:05:08.196 --> 01:05:11.533
Then one day, I collapsed from burnout.

01:05:13.035 --> 01:05:14.286
Oh, no.

01:05:16.580 --> 01:05:18.332
But nothing happened.

01:05:20.208 --> 01:05:22.669
I took a few sick days,

01:05:23.837 --> 01:05:25.881
but the company kept running just fine.

01:05:28.383 --> 01:05:31.219
I honestly thought it would

01:05:31.303 --> 01:05:34.723
fall apart if I quit. Seriously.

01:05:34.806 --> 01:05:36.850
But there are always
spare parts stacked up

01:05:38.060 --> 01:05:39.019
to replace the broken ones.

01:05:39.603 --> 01:05:40.437
Bingo.

01:05:40.937 --> 01:05:42.272
And so,

01:05:42.356 --> 01:05:45.567
I decided to become a fairy.

01:05:47.986 --> 01:05:49.321
You know, it's like,

01:05:49.821 --> 01:05:52.616
if someone you're hopelessly in love with

01:05:52.699 --> 01:05:55.535
keeps ignoring your feelings to the end,

01:05:55.619 --> 01:05:59.623
then you have to put up a wall
at some point too.

01:06:00.499 --> 01:06:02.167
So come hell or high water,

01:06:02.250 --> 01:06:04.586
I always leave work when it's time.

01:06:04.670 --> 01:06:08.548
I guess that's my last shred of pride
I want to keep intact at work.

01:06:09.341 --> 01:06:12.135
But still, you never ran away.

01:06:14.554 --> 01:06:15.514
Ran away?

01:06:16.932 --> 01:06:17.766
Yeah, that happened.

01:06:22.145 --> 01:06:24.481
I was going to propose, you know.

01:06:25.982 --> 01:06:26.900
But then…

01:06:29.236 --> 01:06:30.487
he ran away.

01:06:33.031 --> 01:06:34.074
Who did?

01:06:37.035 --> 01:06:38.286
My boyfriend.

01:06:39.454 --> 01:06:40.580
Wait, no.

01:06:40.664 --> 01:06:41.748
Ex-boyfriend.

01:06:43.291 --> 01:06:44.167
Or, wait.

01:06:44.793 --> 01:06:46.420
Are we not broken up yet?

01:06:47.546 --> 01:06:50.549
No, no. We are broken up.

01:06:50.632 --> 01:06:51.883
Yeah, we broke up.

01:06:52.467 --> 01:06:53.343
So,

01:06:54.136 --> 01:06:56.179
at what point did you start
talking about him?

01:06:56.263 --> 01:06:58.724
I mean, it's all the same,

01:06:58.807 --> 01:07:00.684
dating or working.

01:07:01.184 --> 01:07:05.313
It's all butterflies
and excitement at first,

01:07:05.397 --> 01:07:07.858
but after a while,
all you see are the flaws.

01:07:09.151 --> 01:07:11.903
But just when you think, "I should quit,"

01:07:11.987 --> 01:07:13.155
your paycheck comes in,

01:07:13.238 --> 01:07:15.574
and when you think,
"I should break up," it's an anniversary.

01:07:16.658 --> 01:07:19.119
Then one day,
you have that moment of clarity.

01:07:19.995 --> 01:07:21.705
"What am I doing right now?"

01:07:24.416 --> 01:07:26.042
Yes, I know.

01:07:26.752 --> 01:07:29.463
It's like you said. I'm a coward.

01:07:30.255 --> 01:07:32.716
When something goes wrong,
I look for a fallback

01:07:32.799 --> 01:07:34.426
and prepare for a Plan B.

01:07:34.509 --> 01:07:36.762
But how can I help it
if that's the best I can do?

01:07:36.845 --> 01:07:38.180
What, are you any different?

01:07:38.263 --> 01:07:40.182
You got fired in the end too!

01:08:01.745 --> 01:08:02.871
Careful.

01:08:03.538 --> 01:08:05.457
At your age,
a fall like that can break a bone.

01:08:11.630 --> 01:08:13.632
In this hellish work life,

01:08:14.966 --> 01:08:16.384
will hope

01:08:17.010 --> 01:08:18.011
ever show itself?

01:08:23.809 --> 01:08:24.726
Are you free tomorrow?

01:08:26.394 --> 01:08:27.437
Sorry?

01:08:28.939 --> 01:08:29.898
If you are,

01:08:30.899 --> 01:08:32.567
we should meet again.

01:08:41.827 --> 01:08:44.204
Would you be up for another drink

01:08:44.788 --> 01:08:47.249
at my place right now?

01:09:01.054 --> 01:09:04.641
SPECIAL THANKS TO HAN MYEONG-JAE,
JUNG MIN-CHUL, O.WHEN

01:09:36.715 --> 01:09:37.966
Ms. Cha,

01:09:38.717 --> 01:09:39.551
I like you.

01:09:40.802 --> 01:09:41.636
Are you insane?

01:09:42.304 --> 01:09:43.138
I'm going to quit!

01:09:43.221 --> 01:09:45.265
You have something with Mr. Kang, right?

01:09:45.765 --> 01:09:47.350
-May I join you?
-Take this seat.

01:09:47.434 --> 01:09:48.268
No.

01:09:48.351 --> 01:09:49.728
Then while you're getting caffeinated,

01:09:50.437 --> 01:09:51.646
shall we have a chat?

01:09:52.814 --> 01:09:54.691
Is this why Mr. Kang
asked to see you separately?

01:09:55.692 --> 01:09:57.235
You have feelings for someone?

01:09:58.111 --> 01:09:59.863
You should feel each other out.

01:09:59.946 --> 01:10:01.948
That's why I'd like for us to go…

01:10:02.908 --> 01:10:05.327
Butterflies… I feel butterflies.

01:10:10.081 --> 01:10:12.083
Subtitle: Yenny Kang
